# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide explains how a [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") is organized and how to work with it: how to build one, how to inspect and combine operators, and how to bring two operators into a form where they can be compared. Start here when you write down a Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr "Ipinaliliwanag ng gabay na ito kung paano inaayos ang isang [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") at kung paano ito gamitin: paano bumuo ng isa, paano mag-inspect at magsama ng mga operator, at paano dalhin ang dalawang operator sa anyong maaaring paghambingin. Magsimula rito kapag isinusulat mo ang isang Hamiltonian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") is an exact sum of products of bosonic creation and annihilation operators with complex coefficients. It carries no occupation cutoff. A bosonic mode holds arbitrarily many bosons, so its Fock space is infinite-dimensional, and a truncation enters only when the operator is mapped onto qubits (see [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)). Everything in this guide therefore happens in the exact algebra of the canonical commutation relations,\n"
msgstr "Ang [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") ay isang eksaktong sum ng mga product ng bosonic creation at annihilation operator na may complex na coefficient. Wala itong occupation cutoff. Ang isang bosonic mode ay kayang maglaman ng arbitraryong dami ng boson, kaya infinite-dimensional ang Fock space nito, at pumapasok lang ang truncation kapag ang operator ay ma-map sa mga qubit (tingnan ang [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)). Kaya lahat ng nasa gabay na ito ay nangyayari sa eksaktong algebra ng canonical commutation relations,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"[b_i, b_j^\\dagger] = \\delta_{ij}, \\qquad [b_i, b_j] = [b_i^\\dagger, b_j^\\dagger] = 0 \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"[b_i, b_j^\\dagger] = \\delta_{ij}, \\qquad [b_i, b_j] = [b_i^\\dagger, b_j^\\dagger] = 0 \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two consequences shape the interface. A mode index can repeat within a single term, because $b_i^\\dagger b_i^\\dagger$ is a valid operator that creates two bosons. Also, reordering two factors never introduces a sign, although moving an annihilation operator past a creation operator on the same mode adds a term, $b_i b_i^\\dagger = b_i^\\dagger b_i + 1$.\n"
msgstr "Dalawang kahihinatnan ang humuhubog sa interface. Maaaring umulit ang isang mode index sa loob ng iisang term, dahil ang $b_i^\\dagger b_i^\\dagger$ ay isang valid na operator na lumilikha ng dalawang boson. Gayundin, ang pagpapalit ng ayos ng dalawang factor ay hindi kailanman nagdadala ng sign, bagaman ang paglipat ng annihilation operator lampas sa creation operator sa parehong mode ay nagdaragdag ng isang term, $b_i b_i^\\dagger = b_i^\\dagger b_i + 1$.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Storage {#storage}"
msgstr "Imbakan {#storage}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An operator keeps its terms in four flat arrays, similar to the compressed sparse row format of a sparse matrix:\n"
msgstr "Itinatago ng isang operator ang mga term nito sa apat na flat array, katulad ng compressed sparse row format ng isang sparse matrix:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|              |                                                                                         |\n"
"| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `coeffs`     | One complex coefficient per term.                                                       |\n"
"| `actions`    | One boolean per factor: `True` for a creation and `False` for an annihilation operator. |\n"
"| `modes`      | One mode index per factor.                                                              |\n"
"| `boundaries` | The positions in `actions` and `modes` where each term starts and ends.                 |\n"
msgstr ""
"|              |                                                                                         |\n"
"| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `coeffs`     | Isang complex na coefficient bawat term.                                                |\n"
"| `actions`    | Isang boolean bawat factor: `True` para sa creation at `False` para sa annihilation operator. |\n"
"| `modes`      | Isang mode index bawat factor.                                                          |\n"
"| `boundaries` | Ang mga posisyon sa `actions` at `modes` kung saan nagsisimula at nagtatapos ang bawat term. |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The constructor takes these four arrays directly. The operator below has three terms, namely $2 b_0^\\dagger b_1$, $-i b_1^\\dagger b_1^\\dagger$, and the constant $0.5$, and you can read the arrays back with the `get_*` methods:\n"
msgstr "Direktang tumatanggap ang constructor ng apat na array na ito. Ang operator sa ibaba ay may tatlong term, ang $2 b_0^\\dagger b_1$, $-i b_1^\\dagger b_1^\\dagger$, at ang constant na $0.5$, at mababasa mo pabalik ang mga array gamit ang mga `get_*` method:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first term spans positions 0 to 2 of `actions` and `modes`, the second spans 2 to 4, and the third spans 4 to 4, which is how the constant term, a term without factors, is stored. The repeated mode `1` in the second term is preserved as written; a term is never dropped or merged because a mode index appears twice.\n"
msgstr "Ang unang term ay sumasaklaw sa posisyon 0 hanggang 2 ng `actions` at `modes`, ang pangalawa ay 2 hanggang 4, at ang pangatlo ay 4 hanggang 4, na siyang paraan ng pag-imbak ng constant term, isang term na walang factor. Ang inulit na mode `1` sa pangalawang term ay pinananatili ayon sa pagkakasulat; hindi kailanman tinatanggal o pinagsasama ang isang term dahil dalawang beses lumabas ang isang mode index.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  An operator built with [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\") does not store its terms in the order of the dictionary, so its arrays can list the terms in a different order from run to run. The operator itself is the same, and nothing below that compares or prints operators depends on the stored order.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tala\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang operator na binuo gamit ang [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\") ay hindi iniimbak ang mga term nito ayon sa ayos ng dictionary, kaya maaaring iba-iba ang ayos ng mga term sa mga array nito sa bawat takbo. Pareho pa rin ang operator mismo, at walang nasa ibaba na naghahambing o nagpi-print ng mga operator ang umaasa sa naka-imbak na ayos.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The layout makes construction and arithmetic cheap, with one consequence: an operator can hold the same term several times at once. Sums and products append terms and do not merge them, so call [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") when you need unique terms (see [Do arithmetic](#operators-arithmetic)).\n"
msgstr "Ginagawa ng layout na mura ang construction at arithmetic, na may isang kahihinatnan: maaaring hawakan ng isang operator ang parehong term nang maraming beses nang sabay. Ang mga sum at product ay nagdaragdag ng mga term at hindi pinagsasama ang mga ito, kaya tawagin ang [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") kapag kailangan mo ng mga unique na term (tingnan ang [Do arithmetic](#operators-arithmetic)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build operators {#build-operators}"
msgstr "Bumuo ng mga operator {#build-operators}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The most direct way to build an operator is [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\"), which takes a dictionary from a tuple of factors to a coefficient. The functions [`cre()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-cre#qiskit_bosons.operators.cre \"qiskit_bosons.operators.cre\") and [`ann()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-ann#qiskit_bosons.operators.ann \"qiskit_bosons.operators.ann\") create the factors, and the empty tuple is the constant term:\n"
msgstr "Ang pinakadirektang paraan para bumuo ng operator ay ang [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\"), na tumatanggap ng dictionary mula sa tuple ng mga factor papunta sa coefficient. Ang mga function na [`cre()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-cre#qiskit_bosons.operators.cre \"qiskit_bosons.operators.cre\") at [`ann()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-ann#qiskit_bosons.operators.ann \"qiskit_bosons.operators.ann\") ang lumilikha ng mga factor, at ang walang laman na tuple ang constant term:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the printed form, `+0` stands for $b_0^\\dagger$ and `-0` for $b_0$. The constructors [`zero()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.zero \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.zero\") and [`one()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.one \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.one\") return the additive and the multiplicative identity, and [`from_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms\") rebuilds an operator from the iterator of [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.iter_terms\").\n"
msgstr "Sa naka-print na anyo, ang `+0` ay kumakatawan sa $b_0^\\dagger$ at ang `-0` ay sa $b_0$. Ang mga constructor na [`zero()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.zero \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.zero\") at [`one()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.one \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.one\") ay nagbabalik ng additive at multiplicative identity, at ang [`from_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms\") ay muling bumubuo ng operator mula sa iterator ng [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.iter_terms\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The operator library provides the dimensionless position and momentum quadratures,\n"
msgstr "Ang operator library ay nagbibigay ng dimensionless na position at momentum quadrature,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{q} = \\frac{b^\\dagger + b}{\\sqrt{2}}, \\qquad\n"
"\\hat{p} = \\frac{i \\left(b^\\dagger - b\\right)}{\\sqrt{2}} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{q} = \\frac{b^\\dagger + b}{\\sqrt{2}}, \\qquad\n"
"\\hat{p} = \\frac{i \\left(b^\\dagger - b\\right)}{\\sqrt{2}} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "as [`position()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-position#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.position \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.position\") and [`momentum()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-momentum#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.momentum \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.momentum\"). Together with the commutator functions of the same module, you can check the algebra directly:\n"
msgstr "bilang [`position()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-position#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.position \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.position\") at [`momentum()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-momentum#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.momentum \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.momentum\"). Kasama ang mga commutator function ng parehong module, maaari mong direktang suriin ang algebra:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The module also provides [`anti_commutator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-anti-commutator#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.anti_commutator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.anti_commutator\") and [`double_commutator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-double-commutator#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.double_commutator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.double_commutator\"). All three take operators of the same type and return a new operator.\n"
msgstr "Nagbibigay din ang module ng [`anti_commutator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-anti-commutator#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.anti_commutator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.anti_commutator\") at [`double_commutator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-double-commutator#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.double_commutator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.double_commutator\"). Lahat ng tatlo ay tumatanggap ng mga operator na magkapareho ang uri at nagbabalik ng bagong operator.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"operators-product-order\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mind the order of a product {#mind-the-order-of-a-product}"
msgstr "Bantayan ang ayos ng isang product {#mind-the-order-of-a-product}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two operators can be multiplied in two ways, and they are easy to confuse. The `@` operator is the mathematical product, so `a @ b` is $AB$. The `&` operator is *composition*, which follows Qiskit’s convention of reading from left to right: `a & b` first applies `a` and then `b`, so it is $BA$. The commutator functions use `@`, so `commutator(a, b)` is $[A, B]$. Building the bracket yourself out of `&` silently negates it:\n"
msgstr "Maaaring i-multiply ang dalawang operator sa dalawang paraan, at madaling malito ang mga ito. Ang `@` operator ay ang mathematical product, kaya ang `a @ b` ay $AB$. Ang `&` operator ay *composition*, na sumusunod sa convention ng Qiskit na pagbasa mula kaliwa pakanan: ang `a & b` ay unang ina-apply ang `a` at pagkatapos ang `b`, kaya ito ay $BA$. Ang mga commutator function ay gumagamit ng `@`, kaya ang `commutator(a, b)` ay $[A, B]$. Kapag ikaw mismo ang bumuo ng bracket gamit ang `&`, tahimik nitong binabaligtad ang sign:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect an operator {#inspect-an-operator}"
msgstr "Suriin ang isang operator {#inspect-an-operator}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An operator is not directly iterable, because its terms live in the flat arrays above. Use [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms\") instead, which yields a list of `(is_creation, mode)` pairs and a coefficient for each term. The iterator returns copies, so changing them does not change the operator.\n"
msgstr "Hindi direktang iterable ang isang operator, dahil ang mga term nito ay nasa mga flat array sa itaas. Gamitin na lang ang [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms\"), na nagbibigay ng listahan ng mga pares na `(is_creation, mode)` at isang coefficient para sa bawat term. Nagbabalik ang iterator ng mga kopya, kaya hindi nababago ang operator kapag binago ang mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Several methods summarize the structure of an operator:\n"
msgstr "Ilang method ang nagbubuod ng istruktura ng isang operator:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`get_support()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.get_support \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.get_support\") is the set of modes the operator acts on, [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\") is the smallest register that can hold it, and [`max_rank()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.max_rank \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.max_rank\") is the length of its longest term.\n"
msgstr "Ang [`get_support()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.get_support \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.get_support\") ay ang set ng mga mode na pinagkikilusan ng operator, ang [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\") ay ang pinakamaliit na register na kayang maglaman nito, at ang [`max_rank()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.max_rank \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.max_rank\") ay ang haba ng pinakamahabang term nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  A **mode** is an abstract index that labels one bosonic degree of freedom. It has no meaning of its own: you determine which site of a lattice, which vibrational coordinate or which optical port a mode stands for. The [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") uses the same indices (see [Work with bosonic circuits](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation)), so an operator and the gates that carry it agree on what mode `2` is without either one knowing what it represents. Nothing in the operator fixes how many levels a mode has, which is also why the register size is only a lower bound; [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\") is the smallest register that holds the operator, not a property of it.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tala\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang **mode** ay isang abstract na index na nagla-label ng isang bosonic degree of freedom. Wala itong sariling kahulugan: ikaw ang tumutukoy kung aling site ng lattice, aling vibrational coordinate o aling optical port ang kinakatawan ng isang mode. Ginagamit ng [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") ang parehong mga index (tingnan ang [Work with bosonic circuits](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation)), kaya nagkakasundo ang operator at ang mga gate na may dala nito kung ano ang mode `2` nang hindi alam ng alinman kung ano ang kinakatawan nito. Walang nakatakda sa operator kung ilang level ang isang mode, kaya rin ang laki ng register ay lower bound lang; ang [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\") ay ang pinakamaliit na register na naglalaman ng operator, hindi isang katangian nito.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The occupation methods report how many bosons a single term can place in one mode. This is a lower bound on the cutoff that a mapping needs. It is not a sufficient cutoff, because repeated applications of the operator, as in a time evolution, can populate higher levels (see [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)):\n"
msgstr "Iniuulat ng mga occupation method kung ilang boson ang kayang ilagay ng isang term sa isang mode. Ito ay lower bound sa cutoff na kailangan ng isang mapping. Hindi ito sapat na cutoff, dahil ang paulit-ulit na paglalapat ng operator, tulad sa isang time evolution, ay maaaring magpuno ng mas matataas na level (tingnan ang [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two further checks look at conserved quantities. An operator conserves the particle number when every term has as many creation as annihilation operators. Passing a list of block sizes tests the same condition within each block of consecutive modes:\n"
msgstr "Dalawa pang pagsusuri ang tumitingin sa mga conserved na dami. Kino-conserve ng isang operator ang particle number kapag bawat term ay may kasing-daming creation at annihilation operator. Ang pagpasa ng listahan ng mga block size ay sumusubok sa parehong kondisyon sa loob ng bawat block ng magkakasunod na mode:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, [`relabel_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.relabel_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.relabel_modes\") renames modes: mode `i` becomes `permutation[i]`. The list must be long enough to index every mode of the operator and must not repeat an entry:\n"
msgstr "Sa wakas, ang [`relabel_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.relabel_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.relabel_modes\") ay nagpapalit ng pangalan ng mga mode: ang mode `i` ay nagiging `permutation[i]`. Dapat sapat ang haba ng listahan para ma-index ang bawat mode ng operator at hindi dapat umulit ang isang entry:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"operators-arithmetic\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Do arithmetic {#do-arithmetic}"
msgstr "Mag-arithmetic {#do-arithmetic}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operators support addition, subtraction, negation, and multiplication and division by a number, in the usual operator form or in place:\n"
msgstr "Sinusuportahan ng mga operator ang addition, subtraction, negation, at multiplication at division sa isang numero, sa karaniwang anyo ng operator o in place:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The three terms of `total` were never merged, so the operator held `b_dag` twice until [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") combined them. The method sums the coefficients of identical terms and drops those whose total magnitude is below a tolerance. It is a structural operation: it compares the written factors and does *not* apply the commutation relations. The related method [`ichop()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop\") removes small coefficients in place without merging first, so call [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") before [`ichop()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop\") when an operator can hold duplicate terms.\n"
msgstr "Hindi kailanman pinagsama ang tatlong term ng `total`, kaya hawak ng operator ang `b_dag` nang dalawang beses hanggang pinagsama ito ng [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\"). Sinusuma ng method ang mga coefficient ng magkaparehong term at tinatanggal ang mga may kabuuang magnitude na mas mababa sa tolerance. Isa itong structural na operasyon: inihahambing nito ang mga nakasulat na factor at *hindi* naglalapat ng commutation relations. Ang kaugnay na method na [`ichop()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop\") ay nag-aalis ng maliliit na coefficient in place nang hindi muna nagsasama, kaya tawagin ang [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") bago ang [`ichop()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop\") kapag maaaring may duplicate na term ang isang operator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Products use `@` or `&` as described above, and `**` raises an operator to an integer power:\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang mga product ng `@` o `&` gaya ng inilarawan sa itaas, at ang `**` ay nagtataas ng operator sa integer na power:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result lists the four orderings as written. Reducing them to a single form needs the commutation relations, which the next section applies.\n"
msgstr "Inililista ng resulta ang apat na ayos ayon sa pagkakasulat. Ang pagbawas ng mga ito sa iisang anyo ay nangangailangan ng commutation relations, na ilalapat ng susunod na seksyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The adjoint reverses the order of the factors in each term, exchanges creation and annihilation operators, and conjugates the coefficients. The method [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") tests whether an operator equals its adjoint:\n"
msgstr "Binabaligtad ng adjoint ang ayos ng mga factor sa bawat term, pinapalitan ang creation at annihilation operator, at kino-conjugate ang mga coefficient. Sinusubok ng method na [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") kung ang isang operator ay katumbas ng adjoint nito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A lone hopping term is not Hermitian, which matters when you group terms for a time evolution: each group must be Hermitian on its own (see [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)).\n"
msgstr "Ang nag-iisang hopping term ay hindi Hermitian, na mahalaga kapag nagpapangkat ka ng mga term para sa time evolution: bawat grupo ay dapat Hermitian sa sarili nito (tingnan ang [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normal order and compare operators {#normal-order-and-compare-operators}"
msgstr "I-normal order at ihambing ang mga operator {#normal-order-and-compare-operators}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two products of ladder operators can be the same operator and still look different, because $b\\,b^\\dagger$ and $b^\\dagger b + 1$ are equal in the algebra. Operators that are equal in this sense need not be stored equally, so comparing them needs the commutation relations. The method [`normal_ordered()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.normal_ordered \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.normal_ordered\") applies them: it moves every creation operator to the left of every annihilation operator and adds a term whenever a pair on the same mode is exchanged.\n"
msgstr "Ang dalawang product ng ladder operator ay maaaring iisang operator pero magmukhang magkaiba, dahil ang $b\\,b^\\dagger$ at $b^\\dagger b + 1$ ay magkapantay sa algebra. Ang mga operator na magkapantay sa ganitong kahulugan ay hindi kailangang iimbak nang magkapareho, kaya kailangan ng commutation relations para maihambing ang mga ito. Inilalapat ito ng method na [`normal_ordered()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.normal_ordered \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.normal_ordered\"): inililipat nito ang bawat creation operator sa kaliwa ng bawat annihilation operator at nagdaragdag ng term tuwing may pares sa parehong mode na pinagpalit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ordered operator is returned as an unmerged sum, with five stored terms that reduce to three after [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") merges them. Normal ordering never makes a term vanish: $b^\\dagger b^\\dagger$ and every other repeated factor stay.\n"
msgstr "Ibinabalik ang na-order na operator bilang hindi pinagsamang sum, na may limang naka-imbak na term na nagiging tatlo pagkatapos itong pagsamahin ng [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\"). Hindi kailanman nawawala ang isang term dahil sa normal ordering: ang $b^\\dagger b^\\dagger$ at bawat ibang inulit na factor ay nananatili.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `sandwich` argument sets how the modes inside the two groups of factors are arranged. By default both groups are sorted in descending order. With `sandwich=True`, the creation operators are ascending and the annihilation operators descending, which puts the larger indices towards the middle:\n"
msgstr "Itinatakda ng argument na `sandwich` kung paano inaayos ang mga mode sa loob ng dalawang grupo ng mga factor. Bilang default, parehong naka-sort nang pababa ang dalawang grupo. Sa `sandwich=True`, pataas ang mga creation operator at pababa ang mga annihilation operator, na naglalagay ng mas malalaking index papunta sa gitna:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `==` operator tests exact equality of the stored terms, with no tolerance and no simplification, so it can report a difference between two operators that are mathematically equal. The method [`equiv()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.equiv \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.equiv\") brings the difference of the two operators to normal order first and then tests that every coefficient is below a tolerance. It is the comparison you almost always want:\n"
msgstr "Sinusubok ng `==` operator ang eksaktong pagkakapantay ng mga naka-imbak na term, nang walang tolerance at walang simplification, kaya maaari itong mag-ulat ng pagkakaiba sa pagitan ng dalawang operator na magkapantay sa matematika. Ang method na [`equiv()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.equiv \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.equiv\") ay unang dinadala ang pagkakaiba ng dalawang operator sa normal order at saka sinusubok kung bawat coefficient ay mas mababa sa tolerance. Ito ang paghahambing na halos palagi mong gusto:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The method `simplify` alone leaves the two forms apart, because it merges only identical written terms. Likewise, [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") compares an operator with its adjoint in normal order, so it recognizes $b\\,b^\\dagger + b^\\dagger b$ as Hermitian without further work.\n"
msgstr "Ang method na `simplify` lang ay iniiwang magkahiwalay ang dalawang anyo, dahil nagsasama lang ito ng magkaparehong nakasulat na term. Gayundin, inihahambing ng [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") ang isang operator sa adjoint nito sa normal order, kaya nakikilala nito ang $b\\,b^\\dagger + b^\\dagger b$ bilang Hermitian nang walang karagdagang gawain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Normal ordering is an exact identity in the untruncated algebra, and `equiv` relies on that. It is *not* an identity after a truncation. A mapped operator depends on the form you map, so the mapped images of `contracted` and `reordered` above differ, on the highest retained level only. See [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation) for the size of the difference and how to choose a form.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tala\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang normal ordering ay isang eksaktong identity sa untruncated na algebra, at umaasa rito ang `equiv`. Hindi ito identity pagkatapos ng truncation. Ang isang na-map na operator ay nakadepende sa anyong imamapa mo, kaya magkaiba ang mga na-map na imahe ng `contracted` at `reordered` sa itaas, sa pinakamataas na retained level lang. Tingnan ang [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation) para sa laki ng pagkakaiba at kung paano pumili ng anyo.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Order and filter terms {#order-and-filter-terms}"
msgstr "Ayusin at i-filter ang mga term {#order-and-filter-terms}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reordering the *terms* of an operator, as opposed to the factors inside a term, does not change the operator but can change the behavior of algorithms that read the terms in order, such as a randomized product formula. The functions of [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") return a new operator and keep any group indices attached to their terms.\n"
msgstr "Ang pag-reorder ng mga *term* ng isang operator, kaiba sa mga factor sa loob ng isang term, ay hindi nagbabago sa operator pero maaaring magbago sa asal ng mga algorithm na nagbabasa ng mga term nang sunud-sunod, tulad ng randomized na product formula. Ang mga function ng [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") ay nagbabalik ng bagong operator at pinananatiling nakakabit ang anumang group index sa mga term nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`canonical_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-canonical-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.canonical_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.canonical_order\") sorts the terms into a fixed order that depends only on the written factors, so an operator reads the same no matter how it was assembled. [`order_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-order-terms#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.order_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.order_terms\") sorts by a key that you supply, which receives each term as the tuple that [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms\") yields:\n"
msgstr "Isinasaayos ng [`canonical_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-canonical-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.canonical_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.canonical_order\") ang mga term sa nakapirming ayos na nakadepende lang sa mga nakasulat na factor, kaya pareho ang basa ng isang operator gaano man ito binuo. Nagso-sort ang [`order_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-order-terms#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.order_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.order_terms\") ayon sa key na ibinibigay mo, na tumatanggap ng bawat term bilang tuple na ibinibigay ng [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms\"):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If an operator carries group indices (see [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)), the function [`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order\") makes each group one contiguous run of terms:\n"
msgstr "Kung may dalang group index ang isang operator (tingnan ang [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)), ginagawa ng function na [`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order\") na isang tuloy-tuloy na hanay ng mga term ang bawat grupo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last helper removes terms rather than reordering them. A term that is a product of number operators, $b_i^\\dagger b_i$, only multiplies each Fock state by a phase, so [`filter_diagonal_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-filter-diagonal-terms#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms\") can drop the constant, the number operators, and their products when that phase is irrelevant for what you compute. It changes the operator *in place* and requires a normal-ordered operator, which it does not check:\n"
msgstr "Ang huling helper ay nag-aalis ng mga term sa halip na mag-reorder. Ang isang term na product ng mga number operator, $b_i^\\dagger b_i$, ay nagmu-multiply lang ng phase sa bawat Fock state, kaya maaaring alisin ng [`filter_diagonal_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-filter-diagonal-terms#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms\") ang constant, ang mga number operator, at ang mga product nila kapag hindi mahalaga ang phase na iyon sa kinukwenta mo. Binabago nito ang operator *in place* at nangangailangan ng normal-ordered na operator, na hindi nito sinusuri:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Only the two hopping terms remain. The on-site interaction and the number operator are diagonal in the occupation basis, so they are removed together with the constant. The repeated mode in the interaction is handled correctly: $b_0^\\dagger b_0^\\dagger b_0 b_0$ is diagonal, while $b_0^\\dagger b_0^\\dagger b_0$ would not be.\n"
msgstr "Ang dalawang hopping term lang ang natitira. Ang on-site interaction at ang number operator ay diagonal sa occupation basis, kaya inalis ang mga ito kasama ng constant. Tama ang paghawak sa inulit na mode sa interaction: ang $b_0^\\dagger b_0^\\dagger b_0 b_0$ ay diagonal, samantalang ang $b_0^\\dagger b_0^\\dagger b_0$ ay hindi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation) shows how to tag terms with group indices.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation) kung paano i-tag ang mga term gamit ang group index.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Map operator representations](mappers#mappers-explanation) turns an operator into a qubit operator, including the choice of encoding and the effect of a truncation.\n"
msgstr "Ginagawang qubit operator ng [Map operator representations](mappers#mappers-explanation) ang isang operator, kasama ang pagpili ng encoding at ang epekto ng truncation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Work with bosonic circuits](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation) places an operator into a circuit as an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate.\n"
msgstr "Inilalagay ng [Work with bosonic circuits](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation) ang isang operator sa isang circuit bilang gate na [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started) builds the Hamiltonian of a Bose-Hubbard chain and simulates it end to end.\n"
msgstr "Binubuo ng [Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started) ang Hamiltonian ng isang Bose-Hubbard chain at sini-simulate ito mula simula hanggang katapusan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`qiskit_bosons.operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators#module-qiskit_bosons.operators \"qiskit_bosons.operators\") and [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") modules document the complete interface.\n"
msgstr "Dino-dokumento ng mga module na [`qiskit_bosons.operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators#module-qiskit_bosons.operators \"qiskit_bosons.operators\") at [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") ang kumpletong interface.\n"
